  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri H B Shivakumar vs The State Of Karnataka on 5 June, 2024 -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:19451-Db Wp No. 23526 of 2023 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 5Th Day Of June, 2024 Present The Hon'Ble Mrs Justice Anu Sivaraman And The Hon'Ble Mr Justice Anant Ramanath Hegde Writ Petition No. 23526 Of 2023 (S-Ksat) Between: Sri H B Shivakumar, S/O Late Hanumanthaiah, Aged About 62 Years, R/At Flat No.204, Building No.30, Mantri, Residendcy Kalena Agrahara, Bannerghatta Road, Bengaluru-560076. ...Petitioner (By Sri T P Muthanna, Advocate) And: 1. The State Of Karnataka, Represented By Principal Secretary To Government Of Health And Digitally Family Welfare Service, signed by C Vikasa Soudha, Dr Ambedkar Road, Honnur Sab Location: Bengaluru-560001. High Court 2. Of The Commissioner For Food Safety And Karnataka Standard Authority, Commissioner For Health And Family Service, K R Circle, Sehshadri Road, Bengaluru-560001. 3. Director, Health And Family Welfare Service, Arogya Soudha, Magadi Road, Bengaluru-560023. 4. ASSISTANT COMMISSIONER, (ADMINISTRATION) FOOD SAFETY AND STANDARD -2- NC: 2024:KHC:19451-DB WP No. 23526 of 2023 Sri H B Shivakumar vs The State Of Karnataka on 5 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/116326266/ 1 AUTHORITY, BENGALURU-560001 ...RESPONDENTS (BY SRI VIKAS ROJIPURA, AGA FOR R1 TO R4) THIS WRIT PETITION IS FILED UNDER ARTICLES 226 AND 227 OF CONSTITUTION OF INDIA PRAYING TO a) CALL FOR THE ENTIRE RECORDS LEADING TO PASSING OF THE ORDER DATED 09.08.2023 IN APPLICATION No.10779/2022 PASSED BY THE LEARNED KARNATAKA STATE ADMINISTRATIVE TRIBUNAL, BELAGAVI AND [LEAKAGE_MASK] THE IMPUGNED ORDER DATED 09.08.2023 (ANNEXURE-A) AND ETC. THIS PETITION COMING ON FOR PRELIMINARY HEARING IN 'B' GROUP, THIS DAY THE COURT MADE THE FOLLOWING: ORDER 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "4. It is submitted by the learned Government Advocate that the matter is gaining attention of the Government in terms of the common judgment and that some time is required for consideration of the matter and that atleast three months NC: 2024:KHC:19451-DB time may be required by the Government to take a final decision in the matter."
  },
